Fillets and chamfers: on a closed spine, the p-curves of the pieces cut by
the faces beyond over a gap (0055, 0071, 0142) in their faces' periods
(mitcad#263).

The case: a boss under a plate whose rounded corner the boss's foot
chamfer runs past (0142), the boss's seam, the closed spine's start, in
the gap. The pieces of the gap past the spine's start take the other
contact's line and its p-curve on the boss from the whole blend, and their
parameters a period on: their p-curves on the boss lay a period beyond its
seam, and the boss's wire did not close in 2d. After the gaps are filled
(ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps), each piece's p-curve on its face is taken into the
face's period where it lies wholly outside it (ChFi3d_PCurveInFacePeriod,
0144).

Before, the chamfer of the case gave an unorientable face.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
index bf713193..610133a8 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -5823,6 +5823,13 @@ static void ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps(TopOpeBRepDS_DataStructure&
         {
           FI.SetLastParameter(FI.LastParameter() + Cl->Period());
         }
+        // (Its p-curve on a periodic face then lies a period on, past the
+        // face's seam: it is taken back into the face's period.)
+        const int iF = LSD.Value(j)->Index(s);
+        if (iF > 0 && !LSD.Value(j)->IsOnCurve(s))
+        {
+          ChFi3d_PCurveInFacePeriod(FI, TopoDS::Face(DStr.Shape(iF)));
+        }
       }
     }
   }
